th its southern part in Schwyz and Lucerne.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lake-zurich"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lake-zurich.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lake Zürich</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Lake Zürich is a lake in northern Switzerland, about 40 kilometres long, stretching south-east from the city of Zürich, which stands where the Limmat flows out of it.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/lakhajirajsinhji-ii"><span class="enc-name">Lakhajirajsinhji II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lakhajirajsinhji II was Thakore Sahib of Rajkot, a princely state in Kathiawar in western India, from 1907 until his death in 1930.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/lakhdhirji-waghji"><span class="enc-name">Lakhdhirji Waghji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lakhdhirji Waghji was the Thakore Sahib, later Maharaja, of Morvi in Kathiawar from 1922 until the state joined the United State of Saurashtra in 1948.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lakhpatji"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lakhpatji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lakhpatji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Lakhpatji was the Rao of Cutch from 1741 to 1761.</span></a></li></ul>
